            <ArticleTitle>Hydroxychloroquine-induced acute generalized exanthematous pustulosis with positive patch-testing.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>693-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/0253-7613.169589</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute generalized exanthematous pustulosis (AGEP) is a severe cutaneous adverse reaction, mostly induced by drugs. Hydroxychloroquine have been rarely reported in literature as a causative drug of this reaction. We report a case of AGEP induced by hydroxychloroquine with systemic involvement and confirmed by positive patch testing.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
